  "id": "reel_saraighat",
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "text": "In 1671, four thousand Mughal warships sailed down the Brahmaputra River to conquer Assam. On open ground, the imperial army was unbeatable. So General Lachit Borphukan lured them into the Saraighat gorge, where the river narrows to one kilometer. As the massive Mughal fleet choked in the rapids, agile Assamese war boats launched a devastating ambush from both banks. Trapped and helpless, the imperial armada was shattered. Assam stood free.",
